WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,530 --> 00:00:02,330
Brother, didn't you leave?

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:04,630
Why are you back again? Go in and say yes

3
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:09,330
Brother Qiang, I just went out with a few people to accompany me.

4
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:10,930
Have you seen a little bit of what they look like?

5
00:00:10,930 --> 00:00:12,730
One has a middle parted head and a medium build

6
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:13,930
Another one is wearing a hat

7
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,530
I can't see the other ones clearly.

8
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:17,730
They are not familiar faces at our dock.

9
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:18,730
But it's also

10
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,530
Brother Zhang is in the limelight recently

11
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:21,930
Those people are just jealous

12
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:23,930
I don’t dare to blatantly do it myself.

13
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,530
I guess these people were brought in by other people from the dock.

14
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:30,650
Brother Zhang, what are you going to do?

15
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:31,850
Haven't thought about it yet

16
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,740
It's right to deal with today first and then talk about it.

17
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:39,340
You definitely can't sail the boat in this situation today.

18
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,740
So, just wait for me

19
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,140
I'll take you back on a motorcycle

20
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,140
May 4th

21
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:45,790
Brother Qiang, do you still have this good thing?

22
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:46,990
In our line of work

23
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:47,990
It’s cash flow that goes

24
00:00:47,990 --> 00:00:49,790
I always carry thousands of dollars in cash at home.

25
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:52,190
Things would be really unreliable if I didn't have a guy on my hands.

26
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:56,290
Let's go, brother will take you home

27
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:57,890
Plus Zero CJ50

28
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,290
This is a legendary car

29
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:01,090
Once interviewed, demand exceeds supply.

30
00:01:01,090 --> 00:01:03,290
You even have to find a way to break off the relationship before you can buy it.

31
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:04,890
Who can drive this car these days?

32
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:06,890
It’s the brightest thing on the whole street
